   "id": "T1",
   "judgement": {
    "kind": "answered",
    "quotes": [
     "A path matches a route only as the table writes it, `{project_id}` and `{source_id}` each standing for\none path segment, and a path with a trailing slash added is answered by the framework's own temporary redirect, status 307, to the\nroute's path, which keeps the method and the body. The redirect is decided by the path alone, whatever the\nmethod and before any check of the route, the token and the body among them; the redirected request is then\njudged at the route's path, where a method the route does not have answers 405."
    ],
    "later_state": null,
    "divergence": "",
    "why": "The text expressly requires the path-based 307 before the token check; A5 rule 1 orders authorization before identifiers and the body, not before redirect handling.",
